{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#cor:dc-ch7-2-7","title":"cor:dc-ch7-2-7","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.md","line":119,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex#cor:dc-ch7-2-7","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#prop:dc-ch7-2-5]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#prop:dc-ch7-2-6]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","label":"cor:dc-ch7-2-7","line":174,"source":"\\begin{corollary}[distance is continuous]\n\n  \\label{cor:dc-ch7-2-7}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch7-2-4}\n\n  \\dcref{ch7:2.7}\nIf $p_0\\in M$, the function $f:M\\to\\mathbb{R}$ given by $f(p)=d(p,p_0)$ is\n  continuous.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\n  \\uses{prop:dc-ch7-2-5, prop:dc-ch7-2-6}\n\\sketch The triangle inequality gives $|d(p,p_0)-d(q,p_0)|\\le d(p,q)$, so the distance-to-$p_0$ function is $1$-Lipschitz and therefore continuous.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Corollary</div></section>[distance is continuous] <p></p><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-636f723a64632d6368372d322d37\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23def%3Adc-ch7-2-4\">↗ def:dc-ch7-2-4</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch7:2.7</span></span>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p_0\\in M$\">$p_0\\in M$</span>, the function <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f:M\\to \\mathbb {R}$\">$f:M\\to \\mathbb {R}$</span> given by <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f(p)=d(p,p_0)$\">$f(p)=d(p,p_0)$</span> is continuous.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23prop%3Adc-ch7-2-5\">↗ prop:dc-ch7-2-5</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23prop%3Adc-ch7-2-6\">↗ prop:dc-ch7-2-6</a> \\sketch The triangle inequality gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|d(p,p_0)-d(q,p_0)|\\le d(p,q)$\">$|d(p,p_0)-d(q,p_0)|\\le d(p,q)$</span>, so the distance-to-<span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p_0$\">$p_0$</span> function is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span>-Lipschitz and therefore continuous. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#prop:dc-ch7-2-6","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#thm:dc-ch7-2-8","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-4","label":"def:dc-ch7-2-4"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#prop:dc-ch7-2-5","title":"prop:dc-ch7-2-5","label":"prop:dc-ch7-2-5"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#prop:dc-ch7-2-6","title":"prop:dc-ch7-2-6","label":"prop:dc-ch7-2-6"}],"backlinks":[],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#cor:dc-ch7-2-7","title":"cor:dc-ch7-2-7","tex":"\\begin{corollary}[distance is continuous]\n\n  \\label{cor:dc-ch7-2-7}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch7-2-4}\n\n  \\dcref{ch7:2.7}\nIf $p_0\\in M$, the function $f:M\\to\\mathbb{R}$ given by $f(p)=d(p,p_0)$ is\n  continuous.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\n  \\uses{prop:dc-ch7-2-5, prop:dc-ch7-2-6}\n\\sketch The triangle inequality gives $|d(p,p_0)-d(q,p_0)|\\le d(p,q)$, so the distance-to-$p_0$ function is $1$-Lipschitz and therefore continuous.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-4","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#prop:dc-ch7-2-5","title":"prop:dc-ch7-2-5","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#prop:dc-ch7-2-6","title":"prop:dc-ch7-2-6","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}